LIBRARY Ra3FrameLab
EXPORTS
    FrameLabEnable
    FrameLabDryRun
    FrameLabDisable
    FrameLabStatus
    FrameLabVersion
    FrameLabDumpDiagnostics
    FrameLabSelfTestRollback
    FrameLabSetGroups
    FrameLabMeasureOnly
    FrameLabFrameCount
    FrameLabLogicFrame
    FrameLabWaitFrame
    FrameLabFpsWindow
    FrameLabEngineFps
    FrameLabSampleAnim
    FrameLabGateStats
    FrameLabDesyncDump
    FrameLabDesyncRestore
    ; 2026-09-17 animation-ruler session: three new read-only exports.
    ; ASCII ONLY -- do not put non-ASCII bytes in this file. It was written with UTF-8
    ; Chinese comments once and link.exe (which reads .def in the ANSI codepage) then
    ; silently dropped the line that followed, so FrameLabAnimRate fell back to
    ; __declspec(dllexport)'s __stdcall decoration and shipped as "_FrameLabAnimRate@4".
    ; flctl's GetProcAddress("FrameLabAnimRate") then failed and read/animrate returned
    ; -9999. tools/re/check_exports.sh now verifies the export table after every build.
    FrameLabAnimRate
    FrameLabAnimReset
    FrameLabReadDword
    FrameLabClockPerLogicFrame
    ; 2026-09-17 clock-accumulator session: offline check for the ms-per-frame
    ; accumulator. Pure integer arithmetic on our own globals, so it runs without
    ; the game and without a game process (tests/test_loader.cpp calls it).
    FrameLabSelfTestClock
    ; 2026-09-17 acceptance-criteria session: in-process logic frame rate (fps*100).
    ; This is the precise form of "the simulation still runs at 15 Hz", which is the
    ; definition of "90 fps without changing the sim". FrameLabEngineFps cannot serve:
    ; it reads the engine's exponentially-smoothed display value and lags behind.
    FrameLabLogicFps
    ; 2026-09-17 P6b session: the objective ruler for the SECOND animation time path
    ; (sub_903910 -> sub_8EA220, dt = frame-delta / client-fps). clockrate/animrate only
    ; see the game-clock path, so they cannot show whether P6b took effect. Returns
    ; "animation milliseconds advanced per logic frame" x1000: 66667 = correct at any fps.
    FrameLabBlendStepPerLogicFrame
    ; 2026-09-17 batch-7 session (building-animation root cause): read-only ruler that
    ; measures the DISPLAY frame counter rate -- vtbl[116](dword_CDB750), the same counter
    ; that sub_6F6CB0 (module "StructureUnpackUpdate", the building unpack/build-up
    ; animation) divides by (duration_ms * flt_CDBC5C). Everything in the derived-constant
    ; fix hinges on that rate, so it is measured rather than assumed. Also prints the
    ; current values of 0xCDBC50 / 0xCDBC54 / 0xCDBC5C. Returns frames/second (or <0).
    FrameLabDisplayClock
